## Definitions for terms in this document

Terms are case insensitive.

ocp
: Acronym for OpenShift Container Platform. Also referred to as OpenShift.

ibu
: Acronym for image based upgrade, which is the process to upgrade ocp on a target spoke cluster using an ocp image created from a seed cluster. The lca ibu test suite verifies that this process succeeds as well as verifies the process handles fault scenarios properly.

ibi
: Acronym for image based install, which is the process to install ocp on a target spoke cluster using an ocp image created from a seed cluster that is in turn managed by the seed hub cluster. The lca ibi test suite verifies that this process succeeds as well as verifies the operation handles fault scenarios properly.

seed generation
: The process of creating the image utilized for ibu, ibi, and seed generation test operations. This test suite manages the seed hub cluster which in turn manages the seed spoke cluster.

hub
: OpenShift cluster that manages spoke deployments and configurations.

spoke or spoke cluster
: Single node OpenShift cluster managed by the hub cluster. One spoke cluster is designated as the seed cluster, and the other as the target cluster.

seed hub
: Multi-node ocp cluster that manages the target spoke cluster which is used to generate the seed image for the ibu process.

target hub
: Multi-node ocp hub cluster that manages the target spoke cluster which is to be upgraded via the ibu process from an image generated from the seed spoke cluster.

lca
: Acronym for lifecycle agent.

talm
: Acronym for topology aware lifecycle manager.

lca test suites
: The code for the ibu, ibi and seed generation test suites is located in the subdirectories `tests/lca/imagebasedupgrade`, `tests/lca/imagebasedinstall`, and `tests/lca/seedgeneration` respectively.

talm test suite
: The code for this test suite is located in the directory `tests/cnf/ran/talm`. This code is the primary reference example for accomplishing the goal.

image or seed image
: The ocp image generated by the seed generation test suite which is then utilized by the ibi and ibu test suites.

logs
: Refers to the data the `reporter.ReportIfFailed` function call captures and processes. The capture refers to the `tsparams` fields in the function arguments for `reporter.ReportIfFailed`.

cr or crs
: Acronym for configuration resource definitions. These are logging objects relevant to the goal.

namespace
: A named grouping of crs. These are logging objects relevant to the goal.

acm
: Acronym for the Advanced Cluster Management.

## Code structure

The existing test suites and libraries are written in the Go programming language and utilize the Ginkgo and Gomega libraries for tests defined in the various test suites. Any updates should also use Go.

The existing code tree is contained in the local `eco-gotests` git worktree and directory.

## Goal

The ibu test suite currently only captures logs for the target spoke cluster.

The goal is defined as follows:

1. Add the capture of logs for the target hub cluster, and separate the log collecting code between the target cluster and target hub cluster, for the ibu test suite.

## References

The talm test suite includes code that captures the spoke and hub cluster logs. Use that code as the primary example for updates to the ibu test suite in pursuit of the goal.

Use the `reporter.ReportIfFailed` and `reporter.ReportIfFailedOnCluster` functions in the `talm_suite_test.go` file as an example for updating the corresponding code in the ibu test suite.

## Criteria for success

The resulting ibu test suite should meet the following criteria:

* Only add or update code within the lca code tree.
* Do not update the `imagebasedinstall` or `seedgeneration` test suites.
* Do not update any code in any `mgmt` directories.
* Only update code in the `imagebasedupgrade` test suite.
* Only update the relevant code in the `imagebasedupgrade/cnf` path and do not change code under the `imagebasedupgrade/mgmt` path.
* Report high-level descriptions of changes to be made to the code tree and wait for confirmation before continuing to update the code tree.
* Minimize code updates and additions.
* Prefer updating or adding to existing functions and the `tsparams` struct.
* Use the talm test suite as an example for new or updated code.
* Use acronyms defined above in place of expanded terminology in new or updated comments.
* Added and updated code uses the same coding and comment style as the existing lca and talm test suites.
* Comments for new functions should be a concise one sentence description of the purpose for that function.
* Do not add comments within new or updated code that is within function blocks.
* Update `tsparams` naming conventions in the corresponding ibu test code to differentiate between spoke cluster and hub cluster with the `tsparams` code in the talm test suite as an example. This includes updating the names of the parameters.
* Use the cr variable names from the talm test suite as the reference example.
* Use the existing `tsparams.ReporterHubNamespacesToDump` and `tsparams.ReporterHubCRsToDump` values from the talm test suite for the target hub log capture in the ibu test suite, excluding the `talm-test` namespace.
* Rename the existing `tsparams.ReporterNamespacesToDump` and `tsparams.ReporterCRDsToDump` in the ibu test suite to `tsparams.ReporterSpokeNamespacesToDump` and `tsparams.ReporterSpokeCRsToDump`, respectively, to be consistent with the naming convention in the talm test suite.
* Use the existing `tsparams.ReporterSpokeCRsToDump` values from the ibu test suite for the target spoke log capture.
* Refactor the ibu test suite to utilize an environment variable to replace the hard-coded namespace `rhacm`, which is the acm namespace to dump, keeping the default value as `rhacm`. When the environment variable is unset, use the documented default. Use `tests/lca/imagebasedinstall/mgmt/internal/mgmtconfig/config.go` for an example of setting a default value for an environment variable with envconfig syntax.
* Do not perform additional checks that acm namespace is set.
* Check that spoke and hub API clients are not nil, as appropriate, for calls to `reporter.ReportIfFailedOnCluster`.
* Replace the literal namespace `openshift-operators` with a variable reference in `upgradevars.go`, using the existing comments and code in the same file. Use the variable name `OCPOperatorsNamespace`.
* Describe steps taken in pursuit of the goal with concise textual descriptions.
* Report any significant conflicts or ambiguities found in the contents of this document.
* Report any English grammatical errors in this document and stop any further actions to be taken in pursuit of the goal.
* After applying code changes, report any new code problems for any code under the `lca` directory that was excluded from modification.
